195 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This project focuses on developing an automated sentiment analysis system for customer reviews collected from the Snapdeal e-commerce platform. The aim is to classify user feedback into Positive, Negative, or Neutral sentiments to gain valuable insights into product performance and customer satisfaction trends.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
196 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The system begins by performing web scraping of Snapdeal product pages using Python-based tools such as BeautifulSoup and Selenium to extract relevant reviews and metadata. The collected text data undergoes extensive pre-processing, including removal of HTML tags, punctuation, and stop words, followed by tokenization and normalization.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
197 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E <>
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
198 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Evaluation metrics such as accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score demonstrate that the model effectively identifies sentiment polarities with strong generalization performance. The project showcases how transformer-based models can be practically integrated into real-world e-commerce analytics workflows. Future enhancements include supporting multi-lingual reviews, aspect-based sentiment analysis, and large-scale deployment using cloud-based APIs.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
