314 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The digital age has transformed commerce, with e-commerce platforms like Snapdeal becoming central to modern retail. This shift has generated a massive amount of user-generated content, particularly in the form of product reviews. These reviews are a goldmine of information, reflecting customer opinions, product satisfaction, and potential areas for improvement. However, the sheer volume of this data makes manual analysis infeasible. This is where sentiment analysis, a subfield of Natural Language Processing \(NLP\), becomes essential.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3 4 5]
>>
endobj
315 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (1.2 PROBLEM STATEMENT)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
316 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (E-commerce businesses like Snapdeal struggle to efficiently process and understand the vast number of customer reviews they receive daily. Manually reading each review is time-consuming and inefficient. The core problem is the need for an automated, scalable, and accurate system to classify these unstructured text reviews into meaningful sentiment categories \(positive, negative, neutral\) to provide actionable insights for business improvement.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
