338 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Sentiment analysis, also known as opinion mining, is a field of NLP that aims to determine the emotional tone or attitude expressed in a piece of text. The core task is to identify and extract subjective information from source materials. It's widely used in business intelligence, marketing, and social media monitoring to understand public opinion.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
339 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (2.2 TRADITIONAL SENTIMENT ANALYSIS APPROACHES)
/E (2.2 TRADITIONAL SENTIMENT ANALYSIS APPROACHES)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
340 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Early approaches to sentiment analysis relied on lexicon-based and machine learning methods. Lexicon-based methods use pre-defined dictionaries of words categorized by their emotional polarity \(positive or negative\). Machine learning approaches, on the other hand, treat sentiment analysis as a text classification problem. Common algorithms include Naive Bayes, Support Vector Machines \(SVMs\), and Logistic Regression. These models, while effective for simpler tasks, struggle with the complexities of language, such as sarcasm, context, and nuanced expressions.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
341 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (2.3 THE RISE OF DEEP LEARNING MODELS IN NLP)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The advent of deep learning revolutionized NLP. Recurrent Neural Networks \(RNNs\) and Convolutional Neural Networks \(CNNs\) were a significant improvement, as they could capture sequential and local patterns in text, respectively. However, these models were often limited by their inability to handle long-range dependencies and the lack of contextual understanding.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (04)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (2.4 A REVIEW OF TRANSFORMER MODELS \(BERT, DISTILBERT\) The Transformer architecture, introduced in 2017, marked a paradigm shift. Models like BERT \(Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers\) enabled a deeper, more contextual understanding of language by processing text bidirectionally. DistilBERT is a lighter, faster, and more efficient version of BERT. It retains about 97% of BERT's performance while reducing the number of parameters by 40%, making it ideal for resource-constrained applications and faster inference. Its pre-trained knowledge of language makes it an excellent choice for fine-tuning on specific tasks like sentiment analysis.)
/E (2.4 A REVIEW OF TRANSFORMER MODELS \(BERT, DISTILBERT\) The Transformer architecture, introduced in 2017, marked a paradigm shift. Models like BERT \(Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers\) enabled a deeper, more contextual understanding of language by processing text bidirectionally. DistilBERT is a lighter, faster, and more efficient version of BERT. It retains about 97% of BERT's performance while reducing the number of parameters by 40%, making it ideal for resource-constrained applications and faster inference. Its pre-trained knowledge of language makes it an excellent choice for fine-tuning on specific tasks like sentiment analysis.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
