347 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (3.1 SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE The system architecture consists of three main components: a Data Scraper, a Sentiment Analysis Model, and a Frontend Visualization module. The Data Scraper fetches reviews from Snapdeal and stores them. The Sentiment Analysis Model, powered by DistilBERT, processes this data and predicts sentiment labels. Finally, the Frontend takes these predictions and displays them in an easy-to-understand chart.)
/E (3.1 SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE The system architecture consists of three main components: a Data Scraper, a Sentiment Analysis Model, and a Frontend Visualization module. The Data Scraper fetches reviews from Snapdeal and stores them. The Sentiment Analysis Model, powered by DistilBERT, processes this data and predicts sentiment labels. Finally, the Frontend takes these predictions and displays them in an easy-to-understand chart.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (3.2 DATA SCRAPING FROM SNAPDEAL We used a web scraping library \(e.g., BeautifulSoup or Scrapy\) to extract product reviews from various pages on the Snapdeal website. The scraping process was designed to collect the review text, and associated metadata. The scraped data was then stored in a structured format \(e.g., CSV or JSON\) for subsequent processing.)
/E (3.2 DATA SCRAPING FROM SNAPDEAL We used a web scraping library \(e.g., BeautifulSoup or Scrapy\) to extract product reviews from various pages on the Snapdeal website. The scraping process was designed to collect the review text, and associated metadata. The scraped data was then stored in a structured format \(e.g., CSV or JSON\) for subsequent processing.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [0]
